  <sect1 xml:id="open-issues">
    <title>Open Issues</title>

    <itemizedlist>
      <listitem>
	<para>[2019-11-04] A late issue was discovered where systems
	  using the <filename role="package">graphics/drm-kmod</filename> port built on
	  FreeBSD 12.0-RELEASE will crash during boot.  It is
	  advised to remove the port prior to upgrading, and build the
	  port instead of using the upstream binary package.</para>
      </listitem>
    </itemizedlist>
  </sect1>

  <sect1 xml:id="late-news">
    <title>Late-Breaking News</title>

    <itemizedlist>
      <listitem>
	<para>[2019-11-22] The FreeBSD 12.1-RELEASE announcement
	  includes mention of FreeBSD/amd64 Amazon® EC2™
	  <acronym>AMI</acronym>s (Amazon Machine Images).  Though it
	  also included mention of FreeBSD/aarch64 being available
	  in various regions, it had not passed third-party validation
	  for inclusion in the Amazon® Marketplace.</para>

	<para>FreeBSD 12.1-RELEASE aarch64 Amazon®
	  EC2™ <acronym>AMI</acronym>s are now available in the
	  Marketplace <link xlink:href="https://aws.amazon.com/marketplace/pp/B081NF7BY7">here</link>.</para>
      </listitem>
    </itemizedlist>
